invariant: INV-16
file: srv_auth.c
catches: quic_loop_widemul
reason: the server signs its CertificateVerify with its P-256 key under
  CH_WIDEMUL_NOT_STATED whatever it answered. The signature still
  verifies. test/quic_loop_widemul.h runs the r2 identity, a P-256 key,
  and requires a server that answers CH_WIDEMUL_CONSTANT_TIME to call no
  file under its own names.

--- old
        return p256_sign(widemul_answer(cfg), id->priv, digest, sig, cap, sig_len);
--- new
        return p256_sign(CH_WIDEMUL_NOT_STATED, id->priv, digest, sig, cap, sig_len);
